  "teaId": "joanna-fund",
  "text": "The most famous ministry in history was funded by women, and Luke names them on purpose.\n\nLuke chapter eight. Three verses that get skipped constantly.\n\nJesus is going through every city and village preaching, and the twelve are with him. Standard. And then Luke adds, \"And certain women, which had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities.\"\n\nAnd he names them.\n\nMary called Magdalene, out of whom went seven devils. Joanna. Susanna. And many others.\n\nStop on Joanna for a second, because Luke drops her job title like it's nothing. \"Joanna the wife of Chuza Herod's steward.\"\n\nHerod's steward. That is a household manager inside the royal court. Which means Joanna had access, money, and an enormous amount to lose by being here.\n\nAnd then the line. \"Which ministered unto him of their substance.\"\n\nTheir substance. Their own resources.\n\nLuke did not have to write any of that down. He wanted somebody two thousand years later to know exactly who paid for it.",
